{
  "summary": "Prevent partial overrides of non-valid BlockValidationState instances in two validation code paths. When ConnectBlock encounters a mutated block, it logs the invalidity and resets the state before recording a fatal corruption error instead of mixing invalidity reasons with error modes. In ActivateBestChainStep, if DisconnectTip fails and returns an existing error state, it logs and propagates that error without re-emitting a second duplicate fatal-error notification.",
  "problem": "ValidationState::Error only sets reject reasons if the state is still valid; when invoked on an already-invalid or errored state, it switches the mode while keeping the earlier reason and debug message, producing a confusing hybrid state. Additionally, failures like disk flush errors during tip disconnection currently cause ActivateBestChainStep to trigger duplicate, less specific fatal error notifications.",
  "evidence": [
   "Description notes the issue was discovered during code review of #35570: 'Code review in #35570 found two places where this happens. This makes the in-and-out use of the state parameter harder to follow and to remove later.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
